OL,3,ABayeux Tapestry unveiled to UK public
OL,4,Afor first time at British Museum
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Bayeux Tapestry has gone on public
OL,7,Fdisplay in the UK for the first time
OL,8,Fsince it was created nearly 1,000 years
OL,9,Fago.
OL,11,FIt was originally embroidered in
OL,12,FEngland but kept for centuries in
OL,13,FFrance, and tells the story of the
OL,14,FNorman conquest of England and the
OL,15,FBattle of Hastings in 1066.
OL,17,FThe 70m (230ft)-long 11th Century
OL,18,Ftapestry is being loaned to the British
OL,19,FMuseum while its usual home in
OL,20,FNormandy, France undergoes renovation.
OL,23,APub: 10-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/39
